From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] x1000: h2boot: boot Linux from the SD card by default (Eros Q)

For Fathom on the HiFi Walker H2 / Eros Q hw4: with no key held at power-on,
boot the "Linux" entry (/uImage and /linux_cmdline.txt from the SD card)
instead of Rockbox. If that fails, fall through to the recovery menu as
before. Vol+ (recovery menu) and Play (original firmware) are unchanged, and
Rockbox can still be started from the recovery menu's Boot select.
---
--- a/bootloader/x1000/main.c
+++ b/bootloader/x1000/main.c
@@ -94,7 +94,14 @@
             boot_of_recovery();
 #endif
         else
+#if defined(EROS_QN)
+            /* h2boot (Fathom): boot Linux from the SD card (/uImage and
+             * /linux_cmdline.txt). Rockbox stays available from the recovery
+             * menu's Boot select. */
+            boot_linux();
+#else
             boot_rockbox();
+#endif
     }
 
     /* This function does not return. */
